  "scope": "Controlled Store context, fresh signal scope ownership and existing SIP-primary independent signal regressions on local macOS arm64. No actual private SIP-candidate signal/media routing or whole-clause/task qualification. The current local SIP/Core socket fixture also revalidates original quarantined admission, cancellation and public media recovery; no private audience application is claimed.",
  "implementation": [
    "Distinguish Media, Signal and Presence while retaining exact original native/SIP physical, current credential/key/Device/Endpoint, member epoch, reciprocal partner and recipient-ceiling validation.",
    "Media retains offer/subscription requirements; Signal does not borrow those permissions or codec matching. Existing directional readers still require current named DTMF rights. Pending Signal requires captured applied audience and original execution; sealed current lifetimes do not reuse an ended controller.",
    "Native public primaries with private SIP floors derive the full context and independent external route-owner interval. Presence source validation remains separate from media permission; early native candidate registration remains checked before a physical floor.",
    "Fresh return resolution validates the captured original primary through closure facts rather than reopening the old private media grant, including already captured SIP departure after route revocation.",
    "Public native primary fallback is limited to SIP consultations. Native/native public primary physical metadata survives private-provider closure; its private candidate and actual pair keep their protected context."
  ],
